VeridianOS: KSDCMapping: mark 'flush' [[maybe_unused]]

GCC reported unused parameter 'flush' [-Wunused-parameter] in
KSDCMapping::detachFromSharedMemory() (src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h:150).
The parameter is only read under #ifdef KSDC_MSYNC_SUPPORTED, which needs
_POSIX_SYNCHRONIZED_IO; musl does not define it, so on VeridianOS the msync()
branch is compiled out. Mark the parameter [[maybe_unused]]. No behaviour
change.

diff -ru a/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h b/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h
--- a/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h	2026-10-08 17:30:13.345661744 -0400
+++ b/src/lib/caching/ksdcmapping_p.h	2026-10-08 17:30:13.411008105 -0400
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@
     // completely detaching from shared memory (such as to respond to an
     // unrecoverable error).
     // m_mapSize must already be set to the amount of memory mapped to m_mapped.
-    void detachFromSharedMemory(const bool flush = false)
+    void detachFromSharedMemory([[maybe_unused]] const bool flush = false)
     {
         // The lock holds a reference into shared memory, so this must be
         // cleared before m_mapped is removed.
